# Trivy risk-acceptance ignore list -- SEC-7b (Dependency & Container Vulnerability Management) /
# RISK-REGISTER.md (R-10). Originally six CRITICAL findings accepted by Jason on 2026-07-27.
#
# STATE AS OF 2026-11-06 (re-verified against a scratch build of the current image, Trivy 0.69.3):
#   * The blocking CI step uses `ignore-unfixed` (policy change 2026-10-20), so unfixed findings do not fail
#     the run whether or not they are listed here. This file is a documented record, not a gate input.
#   * Four of the six original entries (CVE-2026-13221, CVE-2026-42496, CVE-2026-57433, CVE-2026-8376; all perl-base)
#     are no longer reported against the bookworm image at any severity, so they were removed.
#   * The two below are still reported with no vendor fix. Renewed by Jason on 2026-11-06 for 90 days (exp 2027-02-04).
#     RENEWAL RULE: renew again ONLY if the upstream authority (Debian) still offers no fix at that date; if a fix
#     exists, apply it (rebuild with --pull) and delete the entry. Mirror any renewal in compliance/RISK-REGISTER.md (R-10).
#     CI outcome is unchanged either way (ignore-unfixed).
#   * The "Full report" CI step deliberately does not apply this file, so both stay visible in the log.

# libsqlite3-0 -- SQLite integer overflow. Status "affected", no fixed version (re-checked 2026-11-06).
# Renewed 2026-11-06. Debian bookworm may still ship a fix before the next review; check first.
CVE-2025-7458 exp:2027-02-04

# zlib1g -- integer overflow / heap buffer overflow in zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6.
# Status: will_not_fix -- Debian has permanently declined to patch this one (re-checked 2026-11-06).
# NOT REACHABLE in this image (checked 2026-11-06 on the built image): the flaw is in zlib's contrib MiniZip, which is
# not a supported part of zlib and is absent here -- libz.so.1 has no zipOpenNewFileInZip* symbol, no libminizip package
# and no zip/unzip tools are installed; Python's zlib module only uses the core compression library. The scanner matches
# on the source package name. Re-check these facts at renewal; zlib1g is essential and cannot be removed or swapped out.
# Renewed 2026-11-06.
CVE-2023-45853 exp:2027-02-04
